    "answer": "Create dp array of size A + 1 filled with A + 1. dp[0] = 0. For i from 1 to A and each coin c: if i >= c, dp[i] = Math.min(dp[i], 1 + dp[i - c]). Return dp[A] > A ? -1 : dp[A].",
    "explanation": "Interview Context: Interviewers assess candidates on Coin Change to evaluate problem-solving rigor, algorithmic efficiency, and edge-case handling under the Concept category.",
    "topic": "Coin Change",
    "category": "Concept",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "code": "public int coinChange(int[] coins, int amount) {\n    int[] dp = new int[amount + 1];\n    Arrays.fill(dp, amount + 1);\n    dp[0] = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= amount; i++) {\n        for (int c : coins) {\n            if (i >= c) dp[i] = Math.min(dp[i], 1 + dp[i - c]);\n        }\n    }\n    return dp[amount] > amount ? -1 : dp[amount];\n}",
    "timeComplexity": "O(amount * coins.length)",
